====================
Download and Install
====================

This page covers the necessary steps to install and run RegReg.

RegReg is *ALPHA* quality: the API may still change between releases.

Installing a release
--------------------

Install the latest release from PyPI with::

    pip install regreg

There are wheels for Linux (x86_64), macOS (arm64) and Windows (64-bit). On
other platforms pip builds from the source distribution (see below).

Dependencies
------------

  Python_ 3.10 or later

  NumPy_, SciPy_, joblib_ and coxdev_ (0.3.0 or later), which pip installs
  automatically

  scikit-learn_ (optional) for ``regreg.sklearn`` and cross-validation;
  install with ``pip install regreg[sklearn]``

  A C compiler, Cython_ (3.0 or later), meson-python_ and ninja are
  needed to build the extensions from source; ``pip`` installs these
  automatically into an isolated build environment.

Building from source code
-------------------------

From the source directory, build and install with::

    pip install .

For development, install the build tools into your environment and do an
editable install (the Cython extensions are rebuilt on import)::

    pip install meson-python meson ninja cython numpy setuptools_scm
    pip install --no-build-isolation -e .

Run the tests with::

    pip install pytest scikit-learn
    pytest regreg

Slow tests are skipped unless ``--runslow`` is given.

.. _Python: https://www.python.org
.. _NumPy: https://numpy.org
.. _SciPy: https://scipy.org
.. _Cython: https://cython.org
.. _meson-python: https://meson-python.readthedocs.io
.. _joblib: https://joblib.readthedocs.io
.. _coxdev: https://github.com/jonathan-taylor/coxdev
.. _scikit-learn: https://scikit-learn.org
